The test added in #5630 is failing now. (I've removed it temporarily and set the PR as draft, because I started to modify it but I'm not sure I actually fully understand it).

@zadjii-msft I have a question about that test: why do we need to have a selection?
https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/blob/84b01c24182be5235bf603431135943f92356d0f/src/cascadia/UnitTests_TerminalCore/TerminalAndRendererTests.cpp#L107-L111

@WSLUser If I correctly understood you, then yes, this will definitely be fixed by this PR. 👍
The problem is that each newline triggers a scrollbar update right now, which has to be done on the UI thread. If your application is printing a lot of newlines really fast, those updates all pile up. If you press Ctrl+C your application will be killed, but that backlog of updates still needs to be processed.
What this PR does is to throttle those updates down to 1 update every 8ms, preventing the application from ever piling up any updates.

